-- title:
--   Quarter-unit theta translates and sixth-order Gaussian error tables
-- statement:
--   Defines 25 positive rational weights, their shifts from −2 through 4, the signed Gaussian–theta residual, real derivative polynomials, rational interval operations, 72 theta rows, 224 Gaussian rows and a per-cell squared-energy bound.
-- source:
--   Masullo RH specialization, finite Gaussian approximations on all expanding weighted windows. The signed residual and the shifted Gram matrices use the mission’s published definitions. The previous factorial-grid proof is https://prove2.me/submissions/770071af-0aae-4bf3-ad37-8d6f2536bd14 . The dataset is provided explicitly in the Lean definition. The integer weights divide by 268435456. The shifts are (i−8)/4 for i=0,…,24.

